    "description": "**Context**\nCertain links need to be reserved exclusively for VIP use, and those links should not flow through to the CMS the way standard affiliate links do.\n\n**Requirements**\n\n* Add a VIP flag/attribute on Affiliate Link records so ops can mark a specific link as VIP-exclusive.\n* VIP-flagged links must be excluded from the data sent to the CMS integration (the CMS does not need VIP links).\n* For VIP links, ops will continue sending the link directly to the user manually (not surfaced through the website) — same usage pattern as today, just flagged.\n\n**Constraints / Dependencies**\nHow VIP links get formally linked to specific sign-ups/players is still open and was explicitly deferred to a future discovery session — this ticket covers only the VIP flag and the CMS-feed exclusion, not the link-to-signup association workflow.\n\n**Source**\nFathom — WagerTech <> Jumpr Weekly Sync, 09/23/2026 (https://fathom.video/calls/831090060) — Joyce Kiddell \\~1:04:39–1:06:05, Kobi Kunasekaran \\~1:05:20–1:06:05. (Not separately captured in Taryn's handwritten notes — sourced from transcript only.)",
